  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Monday)\nIssued at 1019 AM MST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nBlocking pattern will persist as the western NOAM ridge continues\nto support mild and dry weather into next week over the region. \nWeak near daily impulses will support cool fronts through the \nflow, which will keep high temps in the 50s/60s for most days. A \nfew low 70s may be possible at times. The strongest of the fronts \nwill be a backdoor cool front Wed, which will mainly affect \neastern areas of the FA. Upper impulse is moving through the \nregion today and supporting a sfc trough into the area. Winds will\nbe breezy behind the trough with gusts over 40 mph expected on \nportions of the SD Plains, esp the NW SD Plains into western \ncentral. A stronger Central Canadian upper trough will dive south \nout of Canada Wed and support a backdoor cool front into the \nregion. The only impact from this system will be cooler highs over\nthe eastern half for Thursday. This cool down will be short-lived\nas the western NOAM ridge quickly rebuilds into the region, \nsupporting a very mild and dry weekend. Mild and dry weather will \npersist into next week. However, an upper trough is expected to \ndig into the western CONUS next week, and will eventually shift \neast. This will support a transition to unsettled conds later in \nthe week, with cooler weather as well. Much uncertainly among \nmodels and guidance per this troughs evolution and track, with low\nconfidence in forecast details beyond next Wed.",
